{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     theme-switch — the two-state control, for a bar.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     role="switch" with aria-checked, because that is what it is. The sun's
     rays, the crescent and the knob's position all come from `data-theme` on
     <html> IN CSS — so the correct state is in the first painted frame,
     before any script runs, and it follows the OS flipping at sunset for
     free. assets/js/nav.js only keeps aria-checked honest.

     The three-state radiogroup (Light / Auto / Dark) lives in the mobile
     sheet, where there is room for it — see chrome/theme-toggle.hbs. A bar
     has one square to spend.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<button type="button" class="ns-themeswitch" role="switch" aria-checked="false"
        aria-label="{{t "Dark mode"}}" data-ns-theme-toggle>
    <span class="ns-themeswitch__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</button>
